# Minimum cx version - a NUMERIC FLOOR, not the capability decision. The authoritative gate is
# the capability probe in hooks/cx_check.py (`cx mcp bridge --help` + `cx hooks codex-pre-tool-use
# --help` must exit 0); a build that passes this number but fails the probe is reported `incapable`.
# 2.3.65 (GA) is confirmed to ship the codex-* hook subcommands, so this floor is now a REAL
# capability guarantee for the public release, not just a numeric pre-filter — the probe still runs
# and remains authoritative for anything unexpected.
# Synced fail-closed fallbacks: hooks/cx_check.py, scripts/cx-bootstrap.sh, and
# scripts/cx-mcp-guard.sh (search: CX_MIN_VERSION).
# Format: a single MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH line (the first non-comment, non-empty line wins).
2.3.65